 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-23T02:31:44-08:00","id":1433149,"title":"","content":"Is there somewhere official or fan write-up for Greek/Persian <b>Manticore</b> monster?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-23T06:18:17-08:00","id":1433157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1430886-2e-where-are-gods-research-of-gameline?p=1433149#post1433149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there somewhere official or fan write-up for Greek/Persian <b>Manticore</b> monster?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nothing in Origin, Hero, the Demigod Manuscript, or Titanomachy so probably not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-23T08:01:40-08:00","id":1433161,"title":"","content":"Manticores are a mythic reflection of tigers. In many European languages the word is Mantiger. Use the stats for a tiger beefed up a bit and play Manticores as particularly tough and sly weretigers. Alternatively, use the stats for Rakashas (sic). The two monsters are closely related.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-23T22:19:05-08:00","id":1436751,"title":"","content":"Is there in gameline official write-up of Helios, as Titanic self of him? I have a bit argument with new player that in <b>Scion</b> it's Helios that is bad guy and Apollo is positive Mantle of this being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T01:37:52-08:00","id":1436765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1430886-2e-where-are-gods-research-of-gameline?p=1436751#post1436751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there in gameline official write-up of Helios, as Titanic self of him? I have a bit argument with new player that in <b>Scion</b> it's Helios that is bad guy and Apollo is positive Mantle of this being.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some titans are good guys. Helios, like Maat, would be a noble and humane titan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T06:38:01-08:00","id":1436793,"title":"","content":"I have just started reading through Scion: Origin, so I've got a lot to read still. But I'm curious if there's a write-up of Prometheus anywhere? One of my players for the game I'm starting up soon is interested in playing a Scion of Prometheus. I'm also curious how well that would work out, since he's technically a Titan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25528-ardrikk","name":"Ardrikk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-24T07:10:42-08:00","id":1436797,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's an official one, but for a Scion, all you'd need is to agree on one Calling and one Purview that you and your player think he should have. (I'd go for Sage and Trickster as definite candidates, and Epic Stamina for one of his Purviews. Maybe Forge to cover his role as culture hero who introduces new arts to humanity.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries o